---
description: Commit and push after every change
alwaysApply: true
---
After you finish making changes to the project:
1. Run `git add -A`
2. Run `git commit -m "<short, clear description of the change>"`
3. Run `git push`

Rules:
- Do this at the end of every task, without me having to ask.
- Run these as terminal commands so I get the Allow prompt. I will click Allow myself.
- Do not skip the push step.
- Never commit .env files, API keys, or secrets. If you see any, stop and tell me.
